I have been personally working on a soundset for nethack 3.4.3. using the 
method described in the guidebook (section 9.8) for a couple years now. All 
this time I've kept it to myself, and only my friend and myself have ever 
used it. I've thought about cleaning it up a bit and releasing it to the 
public, but I never really got around to it.

Anyway, I thought I'd post a quick topic about it to guage the interest in 
this idea before I put forth the effort of making it readily available. 
Here is some information about the work I've done...



*250+ Unique sounds (mostly from open-source game making programs) (about 
12mb in size)
*300+ Unique event triggers for sounds (triggered from configuration in 
defaults.nh) (all hand picked by myself)
*Quite decent quality (all game related sounds, NO real voices and only 1 
or 2 sounds from a recognizable source)



So I guess that's enough to get the attention of anyone who would be 
interested. Please post if you have any questions or just to let me know 
that you'd be interested in experiencing the most complete sound add-on for 
Nethack I've ever seen anywhere.

One more thing- I use the windows version of the game and I realize not 
everyone could make use of what I've done, but it's a real treat for those 
who are able to try it!


